@yichiche Both are addressed in 49f3f65f.

The `imageio` failure came from `test_pi05_modelopt_fp8_cuda.py`, which imports `sglang.multimodal_gen` but was registered on the `base-b` / `1-gpu-small` lane, which doesn't install the diffusion extra. It is unrelated to this change. #44055 fixed it on main by moving that test's registration to the kernel-unit lane, which collided with fb746818 moving the same file into the diffusion unit suite on this branch. I resolved the merge by keeping main's version, so the PR diff is back to its original six files.

CI is re-running on the new head.

@yichiche @HaiShaw @BBuf @mickqian Could you merge this when you get a chance? Thanks!

On ef3a3014, every diffusion suite in [PR Test](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38519229876) that ran passed, including `multimodal-gen-unit-test` (which covers the one test this PR touches) and `diffusion-coverage-check`. The AMD zimage nightly also passes on this branch ([run](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38473414064)). The only diffusion job without a result is `multimodal-gen-test-1-gpu (4)`, which skipped itself behind the same `wait-for-base-b` error.

The remaining red NVIDIA checks are `base-b` jobs that never ran a test. `wait-for-base-b` keeps failing with `HttpError: Server Error` when it fetches this run's job list, so every rerun ends the same way. The AMD failures (kandinsky6, ipc_a2a, the 2-GPU server startups, KDA, `test_score_api`) don't touch the diffusion test harness, and the ones I compared also fail on main's scheduled AMD runs.

